  "description_html": "Skeletal diagram of the lectotype <b>AMNH 6554</b> of the medium-sized tyrannosauroid <i>Alectrosaurus olseni</i>, known from the Iren Dabasu Formation in Inner Mongolia.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-Mader1989_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Mader1989-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Though a large number of specimens have been referred to this genus, including cranial and hindlimb material from the Bayan Shireh Formation, none of these specimens can be safely attributed as there are no reliable redescriptions and/or analyses.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Mader1989_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Mader1989-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Color_Key\">Color Key</h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFFFFF\" title=\"#FFFFFF\"> </b> Known</li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#CCCCCC\" title=\"#CCCCCC\"> </b> Known but unfigured</li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#777777\" title=\"#777777\"> </b> Unknown</li></ul>",
